{"name":"Hourglass","hex":"#e5e0d5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hourglass","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A clock made of two glass vessels connected by a narrow passage through which sand flows.","A cursor, often shaped like an hourglass, indicating that the computer is busy."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To display the cursor as an hourglass indicating that the computer is busy or processing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hourglass"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hourglass","blocks":[{"text":"An hourglass is a device used to measure the passage of time. It comprises two glass bulbs connected vertically by a narrow neck that allows a regulated flow of a substance from the upper bulb to the lower one due to gravity. Typically, the upper and lower bulbs are symmetric. The specific duration of time a given hourglass measures is determined by factors including the quantity and coarseness of the particulate matter and the neck width."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Half-hour_sand_glass_MET_ES268.jpg/330px-Half-hour_sand_glass_MET_ES268.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hourglass","wikidata":"Q179904"},{"title":"Hourglass (Dave Gahan album)","blocks":[{"text":"Hourglass is the second solo studio album by English singer Dave Gahan, released on 17 October 2007 by Mute Records. It received generally favourable reviews; most critics complimented its electronica sound, while some criticised it for sounding too similar to Gahan's group Depeche Mode."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5d/Dave_gahan_hourglass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hourglass_(Dave_Gahan_album)","wikidata":"Q2601863"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Sanduhren.jpg/500px-Sanduhren.jpg